  "narrative": "The first discovery panel produced three unusually large effects and several small/null effects. Because all estimates are signed to the registered hypothesis direction, positive values support the original claim and negative values oppose it. H6 (MSI-high versus non-MSI on dependency_WRN, direction -1) has signed estimate +0.790 with 95% Welch interval +0.760 to +0.819 and cell counts 130 vs 1870. The raw contrast is therefore strongly negative: MSI-high cells show much stronger WRN dependency. This is several outcome SDs and far above a 10% relative scale, so I accept it. H8 (SMARCA4-loss versus SMARCA4-WT on dependency_SMARCA2, direction -1) has signed estimate +0.784 with interval +0.765 to +0.803 and balanced exposure n=412 vs 1588. This supports the synthetic-lethal paralog hypothesis and is robust in magnitude and sample size, so I accept it and request independent validation as the single most important confirmatory target. H9 (KEAP1-loss versus KEAP1-WT on dependency_NFE2L2, direction -1) has signed estimate -0.796 with interval -0.816 to -0.776; the raw contrast is positive, indicating weaker NFE2L2 dependency in KEAP1-loss cells, opposite to the registered prediction. I therefore reject the original H9 and register a reversed refinement for future testing/validation. The remaining effects are small relative to the dependency-score scale and do not justify acceptance. H3 is rejected because BRAF V600E did not show stronger BRAF dependency; the signed interval is compatible with a small opposite direction. H1 and H4 are biologically important but only borderline: H1 KRAS mutation/KRAS dependency and H4 EGFR amplification/EGFR dependency show point estimates in the predicted direction but intervals include null and near-null values, so they remain active unresolved. H2, H5, H7, H11, and H12 are small or imprecise; H2 interaction, H5 ERBB2 amplification, H7 TP53 loss/MDM2, and H11 MYC amplification/KIF18A are deferred as unresolved because their intervals leave room for small effects or competing directions, while H10 and H12 are rejected as clinically uninformative for their registered directions. Overall, H6 and H8 are the strongest dataset-level discoveries, while H9 reveals an unexpected reverse association needing a new hypothesis.",
  "research_notes": "Discovery results: accept H6 (MSI-high => much stronger WRN dependency) and H8 (SMARCA4 loss => much stronger SMARCA2 dependency). Request validation for H8. Reject H9 as registered; add reversed H20/next proposal: KEAP1 loss => weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Keep H1 and H4 active because KRAS/EGFR oncogene-addiction effects are borderline. Defer H2, H5, H7, H11 because small or imprecise. Close H3, H10, H12, and original H9. Next analyze priorities: run registered H13-H19 if validation does not dominate budget, especially H16 (ARID1A loss/SMARCA2), H14 (BRCA2 loss/WRN), H15 (TP53 loss/USP7), and the reversed KEAP1/NFE2L2 claim. After validation, consider interaction/stratification follow-up for accepted H6/H8 only if needed to assess specificity rather than to rescue borderline small effects."
}

