  "narrative": "No assessments are due at this explore stage, so I am registering new comparisons that are mostly context-specific refinements of the strongest accepted associations plus a few targeted oncogene/p53 pathway follow-ups. The highest-priority scientific issue now is whether the large accepted dependencies are robust to common lung co-alteration structure rather than being driven by correlated genomic or clinical contexts. For SMARCA2, the accepted H8 effect is huge and validated, but TP53 loss is a common co-alteration in lung cancers; the new TP53-loss-only SMARCA4-loss test will show whether the SMARCA4-loss association remains clinically large when TP53 co-loss is present. If it remains near the overall magnitude, it supports an independent SMARCA4-loss association; if it shrinks sharply, co-alteration context becomes important. For KEAP1/NFE2L2, the accepted reversed effect H20 should be tested among STK11-intact screens. STK11 loss is common in lung tumors and can co-occur with KEAP1 loss; preservation of the KEAP1-loss effect in STK11-intact cells would make a direct STK11-co-loss explanation less plausible. For USP7, the accepted TP53-loss effect should be checked among MSI-intact screens to ensure it is not a MSI-high co-alteration artifact. For WRN, the MSI-high effect is already robust in TP53-intact and adenocarcinoma screens; I add STK11-intact testing because STK11 co-loss is another plausible co-alteration context. A large positive signed effect under direction -1 would indicate that MSI-high status remains a strong WRN predictor when STK11 loss is absent. I also register targeted checks for borderline receptor-tyrosine-kinase and p53 pathway effects: EGFR-amplified versus EGFR-wildtype dependency among TP53-intact screens, KRAS-mutant versus KRAS-wildtype dependency among STK11-intact screens, ERBB2-amplified versus ERBB2-wildtype dependency among TP53-intact screens, and TP53-loss versus TP53-intact MDM2 dependency among CDKN2A-intact screens. These are useful because the overall oncogene and MDM2 effects were near the 10% clinical-significance scale or were imprecise, and co-alteration structure may mask context-specific effects. If the context-specific estimates remain small with intervals including no effect, I will treat these as non-clinically meaningful in this dataset. The next validation request should likely be for H6, the MSI-high WRN association, because it is accepted and biologically important but has not yet received independent validation. Existing registered active claims such as BRCA2 loss in MSI-intact screens, NF1 loss in KRAS-wildtype screens, ARID1A loss in SMARCA4-intact screens, the ARID1A/SMARCA4 interaction, TP53-loss WRN effect in MSI-intact screens, direct KEAP1/NFE2L2 effects within TP53-loss screens, and direct MSI-high WRN effects within TP53-loss screens remain valuable follow-ups. All proposals are dataset-level association tests, not causal or generalizable mechanistic claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted core: H8 SMARCA4-loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency (validated); H15 TP53-loss -> much weaker USP7 dependency (validated, CDKN2A-intact and Avana robust); H20 KEAP1-loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 dependency (validated, reversed); H6 MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency (accepted active, not yet independently validated; next validation priority). Closed robustness checks include H24, H31, H35, H37, H38, H40. Negative/closed or deprioritized: H3 BRAF V600E/BRAF, H10 KRAS/RIT1, H12 research marker F/STAT3, H13 NF1/KRAS, H16 ARID1A overall/SMARCA2, H17 MYC/POLR2A, H18 MYC/RPL11, H19 MYC/DHX9, H41/H42 STK11/NFE2L2. Borderline oncogene and p53-MDM2 claims H1/H4/H5/H7/H27/H28/H33 remain unresolved and not clinically established. New proposals test co-alteration independence: SMARCA4 effect within TP53-loss; KEAP1 effect within STK11-intact; TP53 effect within MSI-intact; MSI-high WRN effect within STK11-intact; EGFR/ERBB2 effects within TP53-intact; KRAS effect within STK11-intact; TP53/MDM2 effect within CDKN2A-intact. Also still unrun active refinements: H29 BRCA2/WRN MSI-intact, H30 NF1/KRAS KRAS-wt, H32 ARID1A/SMARCA2 SMARCA4-intact, H34 ARID1A/SMARCA4 interaction, H43 TP53/WRN MSI-intact, H44 KEAP1/NFE2L2 TP53-loss, H45 MSI-high/WRN TP53-loss. Next analyze should balance central specificity checks with H29/H30/H32/H34/H43/H44/H45. Next appraise should request validation for H6 if useful. All findings remain dataset associations."
