{"narrative":"The newly delivered subset analyses mostly reinforce the central dataset-level associations, but they also distinguish robust large effects from small-cell or borderline extensions. H44, H46, H47, H48, and H49 are direct co-alteration specificity checks around the already important accepted claims, and all are large, precise, and far above the 10% clinical-significance scale. For example, the KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 association remains enormous among TP53-loss screens (signed +0.810, 95% CI +0.763 to +0.857) and among STK11-intact screens (+0.801, +0.779 to +0.823); the SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 association remains very large among TP53-loss screens (+0.773, +0.729 to +0.817); the TP53-loss/USP7 association remains large among MSI-intact screens (+0.401, +0.328 to +0.474); and the MSI-high/WRN association remains large among STK11-intact screens (+0.798, +0.766 to +0.831). These are not independent validation samples, but because the effects are much larger than the clinical threshold and are preserved across common genomic and technical contexts, I accept them as closed robustness confirmations and view simple confounding by TP53 loss, STK11 loss, CDKN2A loss, or MSI status as much less plausible explanations within this dataset.

