  "narrative": "The new MTAP/TP53 partitioning largely argues against a simple generic 9p21/MTAP-loss explanation for the USP7 association in this dataset. Overall MTAP loss is near-null/opposite for USP7 (H58, R53), MTAP loss among TP53-intact screens is small and borderline imprecise (H62, R54), and MTAP loss among TP53-loss screens is wide and negative rather than positive (H70, R56). The interaction is also imprecise (H73, R57). However, the TP53-loss USP7 association remains substantial within MTAP-loss screens (H68, R55: signed +0.284, 95% interval +0.105 to +0.463, exposed n=73). This is not a clean causal separation because MTAP and TP53 losses are co-occurring 9p21-region features, and the subset has limited sample size, but the evidence is strong enough to accept as an additional context-specific robustness confirmation supporting the already validated central TP53/USP7 claim rather than treating MTAP as an independent driver. H70, H73, H58, and H62 remain unresolved because the intervals are wide or include borderline values, though I defer them because they are secondary specificity checks and do not threaten the central validated association. MDM2 MTAP tests are clinically uninformative in the positive direction (H59 and H63 reject), consistent with MTAP not providing a broad p53-pathway surrogate for MDM2 dependency in this dataset; I leave other borderline TP53-MDM2 checks deferred rather than closed. The co-alteration strata for the central validated associations are robust except H67: KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 remains huge in CDKN2A-intact and STK11-loss screens (H61, H64), and SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 remains huge in STK11-loss and CDKN2A-loss screens (H65, H66). I accept these as closed confirmations because the point estimates and lower bounds remain far above the 10% benchmark. H67 also shows a huge MSI-high/WRN estimate within CDKN2A-loss screens, but only 21 exposed observations make it scientifically fragile despite validity under the 20-observation rule, so I keep it unresolved/deferred and do not request validation. No new independent validation is requested: the four central associations H6, H8, H15, and H20 are already independently validated, and the newly accepted subset claims are confirmatory context-specific robustness tests rather than new central discoveries. All conclusions remain dataset-level associations, not causal claims or external generalizations.",
  "research_notes": "Current central accepted and independently validated associations: H6 MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency; H8 SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H15 TP53 loss -> much weaker USP7 dependency; H20 KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 dependency. MTAP/TP53/USP7 partitioning now supports a TP53-specific pattern within this dataset: TP53 effect persists among MTAP-loss screens (H68 accepted), while MTAP effects overall, among TP53-intact, and among TP53-loss are near-null/opposite and imprecise; MTAP interaction is imprecise. MDM2/MTAP positive association rejected overall and TP53-intact. Co-alteration robustness accepted for central claims: KEAP1/NFE2L2 in CDKN2A-intact and STK11-loss (H61, H64); SMARCA4/SMARCA2 in STK11-loss and CDKN2A-loss (H65, H66). H67 MSI-high/WRN within CDKN2A-loss is supportive but fragile due exposed n=21. Next priorities are limited: if needed, use H29, H52, H60, H54-H57, H69, H58/H62/H70/H73 only to resolve minor specificity or borderline signals. Borderline oncogene checks H1/H4 and near-null BRCA2/WRN or ERBB2 checks are deferred. No further validation required unless a new central unresolved claim emerges or H67 is later upgraded after independent validation."
