  "narrative": "All newly delivered comparisons satisfy the minimum-cell requirement and are interpreted on the signed hypothesis scale, using the run's operational +0.10 benchmark for a clinically meaningful dependency-score effect. H107 (PTEN-loss effect in KRAS-mutant cells: signed +0.249, interval +0.139 to +0.358, n=61/449) and H108 (PTEN-loss effect in KRAS-wild-type cells: signed +0.273, interval +0.213 to +0.332, n=205/1285) both have lower bounds above +0.10 and are accepted as within-dataset context confirmations of the already independently validated PTEN-loss/STAT3-dependency association. The KRAS-mutant context is smaller, so it is accepted with precision caution, but it is not directionally or clinically contradictory. H113 (SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 in matched RNA/DNA/CRISPR-QC: signed +0.782, interval +0.760 to +0.804, n=333/1284), H114 (KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 in matched QC: signed +0.801, interval +0.779 to +0.824, n=316/1301), and H115 (TP53-loss/USP7 in adenocarcinoma: signed +0.385, interval +0.299 to +0.471, n=290/1132) are also accepted as strong robustness confirmations of central associations already validated at the full-dataset level; they do not create separate new discoveries. H109 (RB1 loss/POLR2A: signed +0.025, interval -0.001 to +0.051), H117 (APC mutation/TMED10: signed +0.004, interval -0.020 to +0.027), and H118 (SMAD4 loss/STAT3: signed +0.011, interval -0.026 to +0.047) are near-null with upper bounds well below +0.10 and are rejected as unsupported within this dataset. H111 tests PTEN-loss/STAT3 interaction by TP53 loss and gives a negative point estimate (-0.097, interval -0.217 to +0.024); its upper bound is below the benchmark, so a clinically meaningful effect in the registered interaction direction is rejected. The remaining interaction claims (H110 KRAS effect modification, H112 KEAP1-loss modification of TP53/USP7, and H116 media-serum effect modification) are not established. H110 and H116 have near-zero point estimates and intervals crossing the benchmark; H112 has a point estimate above +0.10 but a lower bound below zero. These do not justify acceptance, but because their intervals cross the meaningful-effect threshold and the subgroup interaction tests are secondary, they are retained as unresolved and deferred rather than central contradictions. No validation request is warranted: the accepted claims confirm previously independently validated central associations or high-quality robustness refinements, while the unresolved interactions are low-priority effect-modification questions with insufficient evidence to merit new validation. All conclusions remain within-dataset associations, not causal mechanisms or externally generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted central dataset-level associations remain: MSI-high -> stronger WRN; SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2; KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2; TP53 loss -> weaker USP7; PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3. New accepted robustness contexts: PTEN-loss/STAT3 holds in KRAS-mutant (H107) and KRAS-wild-type (H108); SMARCA4/SMARCA2 and KEAP1/NFE2L2 survive matched RNA/DNA/CRISPR-QC (H113, H114); TP53/USP7 survives in adenocarcinoma (H115). Rejected: PTEN/STAT3 interaction by TP53 loss (H111), RB1/POLR2A (H109), APC/TMED10 (H117), SMAD4/STAT3 (H118). Deferred unresolved interactions: PTEN/STAT3 by KRAS mutation (H110), PTEN/STAT3 by media_serum_pct=10 (H116), TP53/USP7 by KEAP1 loss (H112). Earlier secondary PTEN/STAT3 contexts remain unresolved (KY library H96, TP53-loss mean H102, PIK3CA interaction H104). No validation needed for accepted context refinements because central parents were already validated. Use +0.10 signed lower-bound benchmark; upper below +0.10 means unsupported; crossing means unresolved. All interpretations are within this supplied lung-lineage CRISPR dataset and not causal or generalizable."
